# Laboratory Patient Flow

Lab owns sample-to-result execution for encounter-linked orders; keep the lab workbench focused on receiving orders, collecting samples, processing tests, and releasing verified results.

## Stage Sequence

- Order received from OPD, IPD, ICU, or clinical dialog.
- Billing gate checked when required.
- Sample collected, labeled, and received or rejected.
- Test processed and results entered.
- Supervisor verifies or releases the result.
- Critical results notify the receiving clinician.

## Handoffs

- Doctor or clinical user owns order placement.
- Lab tech owns collection, accession, processing, and result entry.
- Lab supervisor owns verification and release.
- OPD or IPD orchestrators own stage progression after results return.

## Hard Invariants

- Must not create encounters or advance OPD/IPD stages directly.
- Must not duplicate orders already posted through the encounter.
- Must keep every row tied to a clinical encounter id.
- Must not hide critical results from the clinician workflow.

## Allowed Critical Actions

- Use the workbench route as the canonical lab workspace.
- May support pay-now or bill-later at order time when policy requires it.
- Flag critical results immediately for notification.
- Keep OPD and IPD order contexts distinct in the queue.

